Looking at this problem, I need to determine whether there exists $f \in L^p(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $\|If\|_{L^p} = \infty$, where $If(x) = \int_{\mathbb{R}^n} \frac{f(y)}{|x-y|^n}\,dy$.

The key observation is that the kernel $|x-y|^{-n}$ is **not locally integrable** in $\mathbb{R}^n$ (since $\int_0^\epsilon r^{-n} \cdot r^{n-1}\,dr = \int_0^\epsilon r^{-1}\,dr = \infty$). This is the critical exponent case — the Riesz potential $I_\alpha$ with $\alpha = 0$.

